 ### Parameters
-*   **Resolution/Half-Size:** The voxel size $h$ (typically $0.005$ to $0.05$) or grid resolution $R$ [S3, unofficial].
-*   **Block Size:** Typically 256 threads per block [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Solid vs. Surface:** A propagation pass may be added to fill interior voxels for solid voxelization [S4, unofficial].
+*   **Resolution/Grid Size:** Determined by mesh bounds and voxel half-size [S1, S2, S3, S5, unofficial].
+*   **Half-Size ($h$):** Typical value $0.05$ [S2, S3, unofficial]. Range $[0.005, 0.05]$ [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Thread Block Size:** Fixed at 256 threads per block in some implementations [S4, S5, unofficial].
 
 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Degenerate Triangles:** If the triangle normal length is $\le 10^{-20}$, the normal is not normalized to prevent division by zero [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Boundary Clamping:** Grid coordinates must be clamped to $[0, R-1]$ to prevent out-of-bounds memory access [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Precision:** The SAT implementation normalizes triangle edges, which can introduce precision issues for very small triangles [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Memory:** The implementation should check available GPU memory before allocating the voxel table [S5, unofficial].
+*   **Degenerate Triangles:** If triangle normal length $\le 10^{-20}$, do not normalize to avoid division by zero [S1, S5, unofficial].
+*   **Boundary Clamping:** Grid coordinates must be clamped to $[0, G-1]$ to prevent out-of-bounds memory access [S1, S5, unofficial].
+*   **Precision Issues:** SAT implementation may suffer from precision issues with very small or degenerate triangles if edges are normalized before cross products [S2, S3, unofficial].
+*   **Memory Limits:** Check available GPU memory before allocating voxel tables [S5, unofficial].
 
